[0.146, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;35m━━━ 5. Chat: capabilities, draft, follow-up, and a claim made only in chat ━━━\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.008, "o", "\u001b[1m$ ./wiki chat\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.100, "o", "\u001b[1mOski Notes\u001b[0m · mlx-community/gemma-4-e4b-it-4bit · local\r\n\u001b[2mCommands: /notes <question> forces a notes lookup · /reset clears the conversation · /quit exits\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1myou ›\u001b[0m what can you help me with?\r\n"]
[13.318, "o", "\u001b[2m(no notes lookup: conversational or editing turn)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36moski ›\u001b[0m Hey Luiza! I'm Oski Notes, and I'm here to be your study buddy for Berkeley Haas MBA. Think of me as someone who has read all your notes and is ready to help you organize your thoughts. 😊\r\n\r\nHere’s what I can do:\r\n\r\n*   **Brainstorm & Draft:** I can help you outline papers, draft emails, plan study sessions, or brainstorm interview stories.\r\n*   **Review Your Notes:** If you give me your notes, I can pull up specific concepts from your courses (Leading People, Microeconomics, Data & Decisions, Marketing, Finance, Business Communication) using the `wiki ask` command, and I'll cite it for you!\r\n*   **Keep Context:** I remember what we've discussed *in this chat*, so you can always say \"make that shorter\" or \"add an example.\"\r\n\r\n**Just a heads up on my limits:** I can't browse the live internet, see your calendar, or grades. If you want me to remember something important for future reference, you'll need to use `wiki ingest`!\r\n\r\nWh"]
[0.000, "o", "at's on your mind today? Ready to tackle something?\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1myou ›\u001b[0m "]
[0.000, "o", "Draft a short 5-day study plan for my Microeconomics final using my notes.\r\n"]
[19.174, "o", "\u001b[2m(looked up 4 note passages: message asks about her notes or names a course)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36moski ›\u001b[0m Okay, I can definitely draft a study plan for your Microeconomics final using these notes! Since the notes cover elasticity, pricing strategies, and cost concepts, we can structure the week around those heavy hitters.\r\n\r\nHere is a suggested 5-day plan. I've tried to build on the concepts in your notes ([N1]-[N4]) while also hitting the breadth of your Topic Map.\r\n\r\n### 🧠 Microeconomics Final Study Plan (5 Days)\r\n\r\n**Goal:** Solidify core concepts, link theory to practice, and practice application.\r\n\r\n*   **Day 1: Foundations & Costs**\r\n    *   Review: Economic Cost Concepts ([N4] touches on this).\r\n    *   Focus: Marginal Cost vs. Overhead. Review why sunk costs matter ([N1] touches on this).\r\n    *   *Action:* Review \"Economic Cost Concepts\" & \"Marginal Cost Estimation.\"\r\n*   **Day 2: Demand Side Deep Dive**\r\n    *   Review: Elasticity ([N2] is a great cheat sheet!).\r\n    *   Focus: Applying the concepts"]
[0.000, "o", " of $\\epsilon$ (own price elasticity, cross-price elasticity) and how it relates to market types (necessity vs. luxury).\r\n    *   *Action:* Review \"Price Elasticity of Demand\" & \"Market Power and Elasticity.\"\r\n*   **Day 3: Pricing Strategies & Market Power**\r\n    *   Review: How firms maximize revenue.\r\n    *   Focus: Link elasticity to pricing decisions. Review concepts from [N3] (Segmenting markets).\r\n    *   *Action:* Review \"Third-Degree Pricing Discrimination,\" \"Simple Monopoly Pricing,\" & \"Price Discrimination Strategies.\"\r\n*   **Day 4: Advanced Topics & Application**\r\n    *   Review: Advanced models.\r\n    *   Focus: Spend time on the more complex models. How does market structure affect pricing?\r\n    *   *Action:* Review \"Oligopoly Market Structure,\" \"Monopolistic Competition Market Structure,\" or \"Game Theory Concepts.\"\r\n*   **Day 5: Synthesis & Mock Application**\r\n    *   Review: Connect the dots. How does elasticity affect the success of a pricing strategy?\r\n    *   Focus: Run through examples like "]
[0.000, "o", "the ones in [N1] or [N3] mentally, applying the models.\r\n    *   *Action:* Quick review of \"Auction Types And Strategy\" and a final pass through the \"Cheat Sheet.\"\r\n\r\nHow does that look? We can adjust the pacing or dive deeper into any of those days!\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
