[7.285, "o", "\u001b[2m(no notes lookup: conversational or editing turn)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36moski ›\u001b[0m Got it. Trimming the fluff and keeping it high-impact. 🚀\r\n\r\nHere is the ultra-concise version:\r\n\r\n### ⚡ Microeconomics Final Study Plan (5 Days)\r\n\r\n*   **Day 1:** Cost Basics. Focus on Marginal vs. Economic Cost ([N4]).\r\n*   **Day 2:** Demand Side. Master Elasticity ($\\epsilon$). Why is it important? ([N2]).\r\n*   **Day 3:** Pricing Power. Link Elasticity to Pricing Strategies (Monopoly/Discrimination) ([N3]).\r\n*   **Day 4:** Market Structures. Review Oligopoly/Monopolistic Competition models.\r\n*   **Day 5:** Synthesis. Run through application examples. Connect all concepts.\r\n\r\nIs that punchier?\r\n\r\n\u001b[1myou ›\u001b[0m For the record, my Kellanova WACC was 9%.\r\n"]
[10.479, "o", "\u001b[2m(no notes lookup: best passage similarity 0.23 < 0.4)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m(guardrail: rewrote a reply that claimed to save or remember information)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36moski ›\u001b[0m Thanks for sharing that detail about the Kellanova WACC!\r\n\r\nJust to be clear, that information is noted here for this conversation, but it is **not** in your current study notes or wiki. If you want to add it to your official study materials, you can use `wiki ingest` later on. 😊\r\n\r\n\u001b[1myou ›\u001b[0m "]
